**Intelvision** is looking for a skilled **Data Architect / Consultant.**


**Project description:** We are looking for an experienced Data Architect / Consultant to help us bring structure to a growing and fragmented data landscape and build the foundation for future data and AI initiatives. The person will work closely with the client and technical team to understand existing data sources and processes, identify data quality and architecture gaps, and provide practical recommendations on how to build a scalable data platform.


**Responsibilities:**



— Analyse the current data landscape, sources, flows, and infrastructure;



— Review how data is currently collected, stored, transformed, and consumed across systems;



— Identify data quality issues, gaps, duplication, and inconsistencies and recommend ways to improve them;



— Help define an approach for transforming unstructured data into structured, usable data;



— Review the current database/data platform approach and recommend an appropriate scalable architecture for current and future use cases;



— Design/contribute to data models, schemas, data flows, pipelines, and architecture principles;



— Support the development of AI bot solutions, including data preparation, consolidation, prioritization, and actionable insights;



— Document findings, recommendations, architecture decisions, and proposed next steps;



— Work together with the existing development/AI team and provide guidance rather than necessarily implementing everything independently;


**Requirements:**



— Strong experience in Data Architecture / Data Engineering / Data Analytics;



— Experience designing or improving data platforms and data architectures;



— Strong understanding of data modelling, data integration, data pipelines, and data quality;



— Ability to analyse an existing environment and identify the root cause of data problems; experience with structured and unstructured data;



— Understanding of how data can be prepared and structured for AI/ML and RAG\-based solutions;



— Experience with cloud data platforms, preferably Microsoft Azure;



— Ability to evaluate different technologies and recommend the right solution based on the use case;



— Strong analytical and problem\-solving mindset;



— Tech stack: Azure, SQL/MySQL, Cosmos DB, Data Pipelines, Data Modelling, AI/LLM/RAG, Python, .NET/C\# (nice to have);



— Strong communication and consulting skills;


**Would be a plus:**



— Experience with Azure, Cosmos DB, MySQL, HubSpot or similar CRM platforms;



— Experience with customer analytics, CRM data, customer interactions, or behavioural data;



— Experience processing emails, call transcripts, documents, or other unstructured data;



— Experience supporting AI products where data quality is a key dependency;



— Experience with data governance, privacy, anonymization, and GDPR\-related data architecture;


**What we offer:**



— Remote\-first work environment;



— Flexible part\-time opportunity (10 hours/week) that can be combined with a main job;



— A challenging data/AI project where you can shape the data architecture, improve data quality and influence how data is used across the business.



— Direct impact, interesting technical challenges, and potential to increase the allocation in the future.



— Supportive, performance\-driven team culture;



— Stable long\-term project and modern technology stack;



— Ability to select currency for your contract.



**Why Join Us**
---------------



We offer a wide range of benefits to make sure our team finds the right balance between work, home and personal development


* Gifts for a birthday and several occasions;11
* Periodical review process based on technical evaluation and English;
* Personal goals setting;
* Participation in Lviv IT Cluster;
* Refund of personal professional growth (courses, platforms, etc);
* Corporate events: regular team building activities;
* English speaking club;
* Game evening;
* Intelvision Talks;
* Flexible working hours (started workday until 11:00 a.m.);
* 18 days of vacation \+ 5 days of fully covered sick leaves and event more (we offer 20 and 22 days of vacations if we cooperate for more than 1 year) with the possibility to take a vacation in advance;
* A comfortable and cozy working environment with motivated colleagues.

For a project in the **automotive industry**, we are looking for a **Junior NX/Teamcenter Designer** to join the engineering team.



The role involves creating and updating 3D models and technical drawings using **Siemens NX**, as well as managing the related technical data and documentation in **Teamcenter**.



Main responsibilities:


* Create and modify 3D models using Siemens NX;
* Create and update technical drawings;
* Manage and update technical data in Teamcenter;
* Implement design changes according to project requirements;
* Collaborate with the engineering team on design\-related activities.

**Working model:** Hybrid  

**Salary:** **3,500 RON net/month**, with flexibility depending on the candidate’s experience and technical skills.



* Technical studies in Mechanical Engineering, Automotive Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related field;
* Basic knowledge of **Siemens NX**;
* Knowledge of **Teamcenter (TC)** is an advantage;
* Ability to read and understand technical drawings;
* Attention to detail and good organizational skills;
* Willingness to learn and develop in a design engineering role;
* Advanced English skills.

Chez Leroy \& Partners, on ne gère pas des dossiers \- on résout des situations humaines. Notre équipe travaille dans un environnement structuré, exigeant, mais profondément respectueux des personnes, qu'il s'agisse de nos clients ou de nos collaborateurs.

### **Équipe soudée**


Nous cultivons un esprit d'équipe fort où chaque membre se sent valorisé et soutenu. La collaboration et l'entraide sont au cœur de notre fonctionnement quotidien, avec des activités de teambuilding organisées régulièrement.


### **Culture d'entreprise**


Notre culture d'entreprise privilégie le respect, la bienveillance et l'excellence. Nous favorisons l'épanouissement professionnel et personnel de chacun dans un environnement stimulant.


### **Formation et développement**


Dès son arrivée, chaque collaborateur bénéficie d'une formation approfondie. Nos équipes suivent ensuite un cycle de formations continues, dispensées par nos huissiers de justice.



### **.NET Developer**


Bruxelles, Belgique

#### **Introduction**

Située à Ixelles, l’Etude d'huissiers de justice Leroy \& Partners comprend une centaine de collaborateurs.


L’étude, assure, d’une part, les missions assignées à la profession (citation en justice, exécution de décisions judiciaires…) et, d’autre part, l’ensemble du processus de recouvrement de créances, de la phase amiable à judiciaire.


Afin de répondre à sa transformation digitale, Leroy \& Partners recherche actuellement à engager un développeur .Net.


#### **Responsabilités**

Dans notre équipe interne, vous êtes en charge du développement de différentes applications pour répondre à une intégration avec notre ERP ;


Vous mettez à profit vos compétences afin que ce développement soit robuste et réponde aux attentes de nos clients sur base des dernières innovations Microsoft.


Votre mission:


* Développement d’applications ;
* Maintenance d’applications ;
* Analyse de besoin spécifique ;
* Formulation et proposition de solution IT/.net ;
* Participation à la définition de procédures et de standardisations ;
* Documentation des procédures ;
* Support et information aux utilisateurs finaux.
#### **Profil**

* Bachelor en Informatique ou Master IT ;
* \+ 3 ans expérience en .net ;
* Connaissance opérationnelle dans les technologies suivantes : C\#, ASP.NET/WEB Api, MVC Pattern, WCF, LinQ, Entity framework, HTML, XML/JSON, Nunit, CQRS, Microsoft Azure Devops, SQL server, mySQL, SSMS ;
* Esprit d’équipe ;
* Connaissance des méthodes et des principes « Agile » ;
* Connaissance des principes de programmation Orienté Object ;
* Certifications Microsoft est un plus ;
* Orienté qualité ;
* Autonome.
#### **Offre**

Ce que nous vous proposons?


Un environnement de travail convivial et stimulant dans lequel vous pourrez développer vos compétences.


La possibilité de relever un défi tout en préservant votre équilibre vie privée/ vie professionnelle.


Un contrat à durée indéterminée (temps plein) avec possibilité d’entrée en fonction rapide.


Un salaire compétitif en adéquation avec votre profil et votre expérience.


Des possibilités de formations et d’évolution.

